course: dictionary
lesson: 4355
title: Gulf: sea, gap or hole
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A gulf is a large area of sea that is partly surrounded by land. It is bigger than a bay. «Florida is a warm peninsula in the south-east, between the Atlantic Ocean and the Gulf of Mexico.» Florida is land, and the gulf is the water beside it, so the context tells you gulf means sea.
explain: Gulf can also mean a big gap between people. Toad thinks «the social gulf between them was so very wide», and the word «wide» is your clue. A wide gap is not water. Ask: does gap fit here? Swap it in: «the social gap between them was so very wide.» It still makes sense, so gulf means a gap.
explain: Gulf can also mean a deep hole in the ground, but this meaning is old or used in stories. The clues in the sentence show which meaning is right. Water, gap or hole? Read the words around it, swap in your meaning, and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A gulf is a large part of the sea that is partly surrounded by land, and it is bigger than a bay.
fact: The Gulf of Mexico is a famous gulf, and «The Mississippi River flows south into the Gulf of Mexico.»
fact: A gulf can also be a big difference or gap between people, groups or ideas, such as «a gulf between rich and poor».
fact: The Gulf Stream is a strong, warm ocean current that flows from the Gulf of Mexico up the east coast of North America.
fact: Old or literary meaning: a gulf can be a deep hole or opening in the ground.
exercise: «The ships sailed across the Gulf of Mexico.» What is a gulf here? | A small pond in a park | *A large area of sea that is partly surrounded by land | A bridge over a river | A tall mountain
exercise: «The Mississippi River flows south into the Gulf of Mexico.» What does this tell you about a gulf? | It is always a small hole | It is a type of bird | *It is a large body of water that rivers can flow into | It is a kind of road
exercise: «The social gulf between them was so very wide.» What does gulf mean here? | A sea surrounded by land | A deep hole in the ground | A bridge | *A big gap between people
test: What is a gulf in «a wide gulf between rich and poor»? | *A big difference or gap between groups | A type of tree | A sea, bay and beach together | A small stream
test: Which is bigger, a bay or a gulf? | A bay | A pond | They are always the same size | *A gulf
exam: Ella says a gulf is always smaller than a bay. What is the right answer? | Yes, a gulf is always smaller than a bay | *No, a gulf is bigger than a bay | They are always the same size | A gulf is a kind of mountain
